# Amrikyy-AIOS Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your actual values

# ============================================
# FRONTEND ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (VITE_*)
# ============================================
# Note: In Vite, only environment variables prefixed with VITE_ are 
# exposed to your client-side code. This is a security feature.

# Google Gemini API Key (required for AI features)
VITE_API_KEY=your_google_gemini_api_key_here

# Supabase Configuration (required for authentication)
# Get these from: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/_/settings/api
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# Optional: Application name (default: Amrikyy-AIOS)
# VITE_APP_NAME=Amrikyy-AIOS

# Optional: Application version (automatically set during deployment)
# VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================
# 
# For local development:
# 1. Copy this file to .env.local: cp .env.example .env.local
# 2. Get your Google Gemini API key from: https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey
# 3. Create a Supabase project at: https://supabase.com
# 4. Copy your Supabase URL and anon key from the project settings
# 5. Replace the placeholder values above with your actual keys
# 6. Never commit .env.local to version control (it's in .gitignore)
#
# For Vercel deployment (Frontend):
# - Add these as Environment Variables in Vercel dashboard
# - See VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT.md for detailed instructions
#
# For Render deployment (Backend - if using backend):
# - Add backend-specific variables in Render dashboard
# - See RENDER_DEPLOYMENT.md for detailed instructions
#
# For more details, see:
# - SUPABASE_SETUP.md - How to set up Supabase authentication
# - deployment-guide.md - Google Cloud Run deployment (alternative)
